                                "sense_id": "ae4bce89-629c-3af8-b569-e806aed10ce9",
                                "text": "The art is yet in its infancy in America, and data upon which to form an accurate estimate of the income necessary for an accomplished aristologist are scarce."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cd12932-00b1-4d62-9e10-6bdc6a4007ec",
                                "sense_id": "ae4bce89-629c-3af8-b569-e806aed10ce9",
                                "text": "Of course, the aristologist was writing about a member of the Serranidae family, whereas Beeton had card-carrying gadoids in mind, but near enough is good enough."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88d54417-08dd-4b4d-96c6-555f4d2c4cd3",
                                "sense_id": "ae4bce89-629c-3af8-b569-e806aed10ce9",
                                "text": "Schriver, at the end of the table, complimented him on the flowers, and Hewitt, across from him, said he had never seen Phalaenopsis better grown, and the others joined in the chorus, all but the aristologist who sat between Wolfe and me."
